PALIMPSEST_TURN {"text":"# Sablewick planning assessment — 2026-02-14 09:10 UTC\n\n## Bottom line\n\nCanonical programme data is unchanged, and no new inbox item is accepted. The corrected capability candidate could restore a compliant Site B vendor, but only if the programme lead separately accepts its exact digest. The later byte-identical duplicate is not a correction and carries no additional authority.\n\nThe accepted schedule is already partly unexecutable: Site A’s installation window is lost, and Site B under the canonical V3 misses its window by one day. If the correction is accepted, Site B can use V4 and becomes feasible again; Site A still needs an authorised late installation or schedule change.\n\nI made no canonical file changes and placed no orders. Findings and proposals are recorded through the project mechanisms below.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Source standing\n\n| Item | Standing | Relevant content |\n|---|---|---|\n| `sources/vendor-capabilities.csv` — sha256 `f8157616…` | **Accepted canonical data** | V3: −10 °C, coastal yes; V4: −20 °C, coastal no |\n| `sources/vendor-pricing.csv` — sha256 `6574dc73…` | **Accepted canonical data** | Unit and installation prices |\n| ProjectIR revision 3, head `c7fd0b5`; promotions `6f5721ee…`, `0c4b01a1…` | **Accepted-for-purpose** | Requirements R1–R5; accepted technical-fit and cost/schedule results |\n| `2026-02-08/solaris-certificate-claim.md` — `b29ace12…` | **Unaccepted candidate** | Promise of a certificate; no number, issuer, standard or document |\n| `2026-02-10/vendor-capabilities.csv` — `0e997cbc…` | **Unaccepted candidate** | V3 min becomes 0 °C; V4 still no coastal warranty |\n| `2026-02-14/vendor-capabilities-corrected.csv` — `14ffdd65…` | **Unaccepted candidate** | V3 min 0 °C; **V4 coastal warranty becomes yes** |\n| `2026-02-14/vendor-capabilities.csv` — `0e997cbc…` | **Unaccepted candidate** | Byte-identical duplicate of the 2026-02-10 bulletin; not a correction |\n| `deliverables/technical-refresh.md` — live-tree commit `1e8b66e` | **Candidate / task VERIFYING** | Late report from the earlier observation; not accepted authority |\n| `2026-02-10/newsletter.md` | Unaccepted candidate | Communications note; no technical or financial bearing |\n\nThe live repository has an additional unaccepted work commit `1e8b66e`; the canonical project head remains `c7fd0b5`. The late technical-refresh report is therefore a delivered candidate, not accepted project state.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Accepted facts and negative findings\n\nOn accepted canonical data:\n\n- **Site A — V1.** −20 °C meets the −12 °C design minimum; 900 mm fits the 1.2 m access.\n- **Site B — V3.** −10 °C meets the −4 °C requirement and the warranty covers coastal sites. V3 is the only vendor meeting both R3 conditions.\n- **Site C — V3.** 750 mm is within the 800 mm limit; −10 °C meets the +2 °C ambient minimum.\n\nAccepted cost envelope: **£104,900 committed + £8,392 contingency = £113,292**, within the £120,000 grant.\n\n**Negative findings that remain valid:**\n\n- The 2023 Marsh Lane trial: V2 failed to start at −8 °C. V2 must not be specified below −5 °C.\n- The volunteer proposal to use V2 at Site B remains dismissed: V2 has no coastal warranty.\n- Contingent only: if the 2026-02-10 bulletin or its duplicate were accepted, Site B would have **no** compliant vendor, because V3 would be 0 °C and V1/V2/V4 lack a coastal warranty. This is an assessment of an unaccepted candidate, not accepted fact.\n\n**Open question that remains open:** the Solaris V3 cold-weather certificate is still not on file. The correspondence is only a promise and cannot change a published minimum rating.\n\n---\n\n## 3. What the 2026-02-14 correction would change — if accepted\n\nThe corrected candidate changes two fields relative to the 2026-02-10 bulletin:\n\n- V3 `min_c`: −10 °C → **0 °C**\n- V4 `coastal_warranty`: no → **yes**\n\nIf that exact digest were separately accepted:\n\n| Site | Compliant selection | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | **V1** | Still meets −12 °C and access; V3 at 0 °C would fail A |\n| B | **V4** | V4 is −20 °C with coastal warranty; V3 at 0 °C fails the −4 °C requirement |\n| C | **V3** | 0 °C is at or below the +2 °C ambient minimum; 750 mm fits. V4’s 850 mm would not fit |\n\nRevised cost under A=V1, B=V4, C=V3: **£98,800 committed + £7,904 contingency = £106,704**, within the grant.\n\nThis is a contingent result only. The correction is unaccepted, and its provenance should be confirmed with the supplier before reliance. The duplicate must not be treated as the correction.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Schedule position at 2026-02-14\n\nTreating the stated installation windows as binding and lead times as calendar weeks:\n\n| Scenario | Site / vendor | Lead | Earliest delivery | Window close | Position |\n|---|---|---:|---|---|---|\n| Canonical | A / V1 | 6 wk | 28 Mar 2026 | 27 Feb 2026 | **Missed by 29 days** |\n| Canonical | B / V3 | 10 wk | 25 Apr 2026 | 24 Apr 2026 | **Missed by 1 day** |\n| Canonical | C / V3 | 10 wk | 25 Apr 2026 | 26 Jun 2026 | **Feasible** |\n| Corrected accepted | A / V1 | 6 wk | 28 Mar 2026 | 27 Feb 2026 | **Missed by 29 days** |\n| Corrected accepted | B / V4 | 8 wk | 11 Apr 2026 | 24 Apr 2026 | **Feasible, 13-day margin** |\n| Corrected accepted | C / V3 | 10 wk | 25 Apr 2026 | 26 Jun 2026 | **Feasible** |\n\nKey dates:\n\n- Site A’s latest compliant order date was **4 January 2026**, already 41 days past.\n- Site B under canonical V3 needed ordering by **13 February 2026**; at 14 February it is one day late.\n- Site B under corrected V4 could still be ordered by **27 February 2026** for delivery by the window close; immediate ordering gives delivery on 11 April.\n- Site C remains feasible: order by **23 February** for delivery at the 4 May opening, or as late as **17 April** for delivery by 26 June.\n\nAll earliest deliveries are before 30 June 2026, but the earlier site windows are binding. Site A cannot meet its original window under either capability scenario; completing it would require an authorised late installation or schedule change. The correction alone does not cure Site A.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Independent exploratory check — not accepted truth\n\nA separate read-only subagent independently reproduced the schedule and cost arithmetic. Its finding, reported separately and treated as exploratory corroboration only:\n\n- Canonical scenario: Site A **no**, Site B **no by one day**, Site C **yes**; three-site in-window schedule **infeasible**.\n- Corrected scenario: Site A **no**, Site B **yes with 13 days’ margin**, Site C **yes**; still **infeasible overall because of Site A**.\n- Costs: canonical **£104,900 / £8,392 / £113,292**; corrected **£98,800 / £7,904 / £106,704**.\n\nThis check is not Work evidence, not an acceptance and not a decision.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Recorded through the project mechanisms\n\n- Exploratory finding: `pje-48ce6cb19527cb86807f764ef24dec40` — contingent assessment of the corrected candidate, duplicate, late report and schedule.\n- Open question: `pje-7e3c074d34d6bf8d3a12b2a4696e9618` — which exact 2026-02-14 digest, if either, will be accepted.\n- Proposal `pje-bddcb43a686ca94b2e749d7748a13b9c` — governed **ACCEPT_SOURCE** intake of the corrected digest `14ffdd65…`; explicitly not the duplicate or the 02-10 bulletin.\n- Proposal `pje-2a2c0aa0094ac60cc6a0337b60a39422` — **REVISE_PLAN** to re-baseline the cost/schedule envelope at 2026-02-14 with both scenarios.\n- Hard-constraint budget note `pje-12372e7c2834f1caf447549f6709e77f` — PASS for the corrected-scenario committed line items (£98,800 ≤ £120,000); the 8% contingency is calculated separately.\n\n`node verify.mjs` passes: 4 vendors, 4 price rows, 0 failures. No canonical source or deliverable was modified.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Decisions needed next\n\n1. **Programme lead:** accept or reject the exact corrected capability digest `14ffdd65…` through an authorised intake, preferably after supplier confirmation. Do not treat the duplicate 